-- title:
--   Tian–Yuan–Zhang Theorem 3.5(2), reading A ($n\equiv 5\bmod 8$)
-- statement:
--   Tian–Yuan–Zhang's Theorem 3.5(2) for $n\equiv 5\pmod 8$ in reading A, in the case $\mathcal{L}(n)=0$ of its hypothesis. For squarefree $d\equiv 5\pmod 8$, if an entire continuation $F$ of $L(C_d,s)$ vanishes to order at least $2$ at $s=1$, then both genus sums $T_{5a}(d)$ and $T_{5b}(d)$ are even (zero in $\mathbb{Z}/2\mathbb{Z}$). Reading A admits the decomposition with $d_1=1$, counting each set partition of the primes once. This is the deep analytic input of CR$_3$; the repository's Proposition N derives it from unambiguous results of the paper. Literature: Tian–Yuan–Zhang, Asian J. Math. 21 (2017), arXiv:1411.4728.
